(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: SCHEME FOR PROMOTION OF MANUFACTURING OF ELECTRONIC COMPONENTS AND SEMICONDUCTORS \(SPECS\) / IFCI / MEITY) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Financial incentive of 25% on capital expenditure for the manufacturing of) Tj
T*
(identified electronic components, semiconductor packaging, display) Tj
T*
(fabrication, and active components.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. Investment in new manufacturing unit or expansion of existing units for) Tj
T*
(   eligible electronic items.) Tj
T*
(2. Minimum capital expenditure investment threshold ranges from Rs. 5 Crore to) Tj
T*
(   Rs. 1,000 Crore depending on product category.) Tj
T*
(3. Application must be submitted prior to placing orders for plant and) Tj
T*
(   machinery.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. 25% financial incentive on eligible capital expenditure for plant,) Tj
T*
(   machinery, equipment, associated utilities, and clean room facilities.) Tj
T*
(2. Concession or margin money subsidy rate of 25.0 % subsidy.) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 25.00 Crore per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. Detailed Project Report \(DPR\) with technical process flow) Tj
T*
(2. Chartered Accountant / Engineer certificates on eligible capex) Tj
T*
(3. Purchase orders, bills of entry, and commissioning certificates) Tj
T*
(4. GST returns and plant layout approvals) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via MeitY SPECS portal) Tj
T*
